{"case_id":"C032","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["missing semantic correctness oracle"],"confidence":93,"affected_functions":["wuffs_private_impl__swizzle_ya_nonpremul__ya_nonpremul__src_over","fuzz_swizzle_interleaved_from_slice"],"reason":"H0 can select WUFFS_BASE__PIXEL_FORMAT__YA_NONPREMUL for both source and destination with WUFFS_BASE__PIXEL_BLEND__SRC_OVER, so it can reach the changed production function with fuzz-derived source and destination bytes. However, it only checks that wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__swizzle_interleaved_from_slice does not crash. It ignores the returned pixel count and never validates the resulting YA bytes. Therefore, errors in the changed composite-and-narrow operation, including the value written from (uint16_t)(c0 >> 16), can survive without detection.","evidence":["pixfmts includes WUFFS_BASE__PIXEL_FORMAT__YA_NONPREMUL for independently selected dst_pixfmt and src_pixfmt.","blends includes WUFFS_BASE__PIXEL_BLEND__SRC_OVER.","fuzz_swizzle_interleaved_from_slice fills dst_slice and src_slice from fuzz input before invoking wuffs_base__pixel_swizzler__swizzle_interleaved_from_slice.","The harness comment states its objective is that the call \"will not crash\" and the call's return value is discarded.","The changed function computes c0 with wuffs_private_impl__composite_nonpremul_nonpremul_u32_axxx and writes (uint16_t)(c0 >> 16), but H0 performs no reference comparison or output invariant check for those bytes."],"recommended_action":"Add a focused YA_NONPREMUL-to-YA_NONPREMUL SRC_OVER semantic check that compares the produced pixels and returned count against an independent per-pixel reference, including boundary alpha/luma values and odd or unequal source and destination lengths."}
